  "body": "M7.3 (4/6): camcraft-motion now reads and cuts stock only through the `Stock` / `Columns` seam. It names no `Dexel` outside tests.\n\n## What changed\n- **Masks:** `pocket3d_prev`, `pocket3d_with_rest_prev`, `pocket3d_offset_prev`, `pocket3d_offset_with_rest_prev` and `multiaxis_rough_prev` take `Option<&Columns<'_>>` instead of `Option<&Dexel>`. The app (`operation/generate.rs`) wraps its program-ahead grid with `Columns::of_grid`, which borrows and does not clone, as #595 did.\n- **Motion's own sims** (`sim_of`, `run_rest`, `optimize_feed`, `quality::{stock_for, measure, rest_area}`) hold a `Stock` on `Backend::Column`.\n  - They read through `Columns`: `above` for the rest and mask targets, `top_over` for the feed sampler and the contact rim, `top_at`/`center` for `rest_area`.\n  - They score with `Stock::measure`.\n  - `optimize_feed` now goes through `engagement_on`; the private `engagement` is gone.\n- **New seam ops** in `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/backend_edit.rs`:\n  - `Stock::subtract_flat`, `Stock::cut_chord` and `Stock::set_tops`. On the column arm each one is the old `Dexel` call, unchanged.\n  - On the field arm, the flat tool cuts with the spanning flank. `set_tops` refuses by name (`SET_TOPS_FIELD_REFUSAL`).\n  - A posed cutting move is refused on both arms (`POSED_REFUSAL`).\n  - `Columns::to_stock` gives the rest pass its owned copy of the mask. This is the same clone `run_rest` already made.\n- **`Result` returns:** `quality::measure` and `quality::rest_area` now return `Result`, because a seam cut can refuse. That is test-only API (the yardstick).\n- **Decision:** recorded in `docs/decisions/587-motion-onto-stock.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- **Goldens are byte-identical.** No golden file changed, and none was re-blessed.\n  - `golden_cl`: 24/24.\n  - All motion suites, including `finish3d`, `multiaxis_rough`, `machining3d` (rough/rest), `adaptive_hsm`, `pocket3d_hsm`, `one_descent` and `quality` (unit): 685 passed, 0 failed (macOS debug).\n  - `stock_engine_agreement` (release, `--include-ignored`): 3/3 (`both_engines_judge_every_golden_program_alike`, `the_feed_sampler_reads_every_golden_program_alike`, `the_pocket3d_consumers_read_both_engines_alike`).\n- **Pinning tests:**\n  - `stock_seam::motion_names_no_dexel_outside_tests` (new): a source scan of `crates/motion/src`, skipping `tests.rs` files and `tests/` dirs.\n  - `machining3d::tests::the_sampler_reads_both_stock_engines_alike` now asserts that `engagement_on` equals the old direct `Dexel` read, bit for bit.\n- **Clippy:** `-D warnings` is clean on camcraft-sim, camcraft-motion and camcraft-app (all targets).\n- **Linux batch gate:** green, 0 failed. It covered geometry, cl, tools, post, sim, motion (finish3d, flow, pivot5d included), app (center_cut_multiaxis included), ui and clippy.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The field arm of the new `subtract_flat`, `cut_chord` and `set_tops` has no caller yet. Motion builds on the column arm, so goldens stay byte-identical. The field arm becomes live when 6/6 (the retirement) switches the backend.\n\nChangelog: none (behaviour-neutral refactor)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFork synced at v0.16.0.\n\nFixes #587\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
